WEBVTT

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.980
The train will be stopping in five minutes.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.560
Please check to be sure you have your belongings.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.460
And have a good stay in the Big Apple.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:10.840
Thank you.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.760
Well, here we are.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.480
And nice meeting you, too, Mrs. Tobin.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.380
Please look us up.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:21.720
We're in the phone book.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.740
Dr. Philip Stewart, in Riverdale.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:25.640
Your son?

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.980
That's right. And have a good time in New York.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.380
And don't be so independent.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.020
You're very lucky to have a caring family.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.820
When can we go fishing?

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.520
I'm ready, Grandpa. You name the day.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:01.160
That's a great idea, Grandpa!

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.680
Philip needs a day off.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.000
Let's give him our presents--now.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:05.960
Good idea.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.600
And this one's from me.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.580
Richard, these are terrific pictures.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.940
This one really brings back memories.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.240
You remember that day, Robbie?

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:06.640
I miss her very much.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:09.780
She feels bad, too, Grandpa.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.040
She called to say the plane was delayed.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.240
You know airports.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.540
I can't wait to see her.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.860
She looks just like Grandma at that age.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:27.060
I started traveling twenty-four hours ago.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.260
Don't you want something to eat?

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:37.880
No, thanks.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.300
After a good night's sleep, I'll enjoy breakfast even more.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:43.260
Well, come on, Dad.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.040
Ellen and I'll take you to your room.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.820
I'm sure glad you're here, Grandpa.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:49.600
Pleasant dreams.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:07.910
Philip, do you have the key to the trunk?

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.300
I have the key, but it doesn't work.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.460
I sent the wrong key.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:36.580
I have something for you. I made it myself.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.760
I think you'll enjoy it.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.920
I researched it for over a year.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:55.600
Fabulous!

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:03.620
Lots of interesting information about our family.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.740
A gift from me.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.800
Thank you so much.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.520
Grandpa! Grandpa!

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.740
Oh, Grandpa, I'm so happy to see you!

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:21.900
Oh, you look so beautiful, Susan. My granddaughter.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:26.120
Like I always said, you look just like Grandma.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:31.260
I think you're going to be very happy here with us.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.460
I know you will.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:37.060
I don't feel alone anymore.
